<title>FINLAND: Finnish EMU changeover plan due for release on April 16.</title>
<headline>Finnish EMU changeover plan due for release on April 16.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland will publish on April 16 its national plan of measures to be taken to prepare for membership of the third stage of economic and monetary union, a senior finance ministry official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The so called EMU changeover plan will be updated every six months, Rauno Niinimaki, head of the ministry's EMU project, told a news conference. He declined to give details of the contents of the report.</p>
<p>Of the EU's 15 member countries only the Netherlands and Belgium have so far published their own national changeover plans, he said.</p>
</text>
